      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOVERATO (9) brings the most attractive profile despite resuming. Her last two runs were in the G1 Queensland Oaks and G2 The Roses, both behind Fireball Miss. She was only beaten 3.5L in the Oaks after interference in the straight. Fitted with two trials and with only 52kg on her back she will take plenty of holding out. GRAND IMPACT (1) is the proven race-fit danger after consecutive Rosehill seconds, including a narrow defeat as odds-on favourite behind Lisztomania last time, who's now off to the Kozzy. Will settle ahead of SOVERATO and attempt to keep her at bay. BOOM TORQUE (6) hasn't won for a very long time but was much better last time at Doomben when 2flashing home into a close fifth. Gets significant weight relief and is worth keeping onside. SIR ARTIE (4) is a tricky one to catch but shoulders peaks at this weight that can threaten. Backs up quickly and is in the mix. WARBY (5) is always one to keep safe for a minor spot.",
